 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+Specifies the maximum number of ranges to return, defaults to unlimited. Only
+valid ranges are counted (after combining, if `combine` is `true`). When there
+are more ranges than `limit`, they are collapsed into a single range spanning
+the lowest start to the highest end, so the response can be served as a single
+range rather than multipart. Values that are not a number of at least `1` are
+ignored.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(100, 'bytes=0-1,10-20,50-60', { limit: 2 })
+// => [
+//      { start: 0, end: 60 }
+//    ]
+```
+
